      "type": "review-note",
      "reviewer": "OpenAI Codex",
      "reviewedAt": "2026-08-24T12:30:55Z",
      "note": "Reviewed the selected exploit receipt and call trace, the commit-pinned reproduction, the deployment transaction, the exploit-time implementation slot, and a complete Upgraded-event query from proxy deployment through the exploit. Calls to pool proxy 0x4658ea7e9960d6158a261104aaa160cc953bb6ba delegate to 0xe5c84c7630a505b6adf69b5594d0ff7fedd5f447. The vulnerable accounting reduces full liability when a withdrawal is only partly paid from available cash, which lets the attacker distort coverage ratios and receive favorable slippage in both swap directions. Three Upgraded events exist; the final event is log 18 of 0x53ac2df1a06dbc6406aceb9ace784c8530c2b279bb6b04de77e7da6537bbefdb and selects the recorded implementation. The selected transaction nets the attack contract 23,564.213231457049370005 WAVAX and 20,873.980832851904983452 sAVAX; the incident loss records CertiK's $2.23 million aggregate across all three related exploit transactions."
    },
